description:
Objective: stop the orchestrator reporting an agent as SPAWNED when the spawn refused and no process was ever created.

MEASURED DEFECT, verified on current bytes at apps/daemon/src/orchestrator/agent-wrapper.ts:226-231:

    const exit = config.spawnAgent({
      credential: secret, expiresAt, kind: step.kind,
      mission: missionText, sessionId, workItemId, workspace,
    }).catch(() => undefined).then(() => { active.delete(workItemId); });
    active.set(workItemId, exit);
    return { kind: step.kind, outcome: "SPAWNED", sessionId, workItemId };

`.catch(() => undefined)` swallows EVERY rejection — no code, no log, no record — and `outcome: "SPAWNED"` is returned unconditionally, without consulting the promise at all. When the spawn refuses, the board is told an agent is running that does not exist. That is a fail-open on the orchestration path: a leaked file is recoverable, a phantom SPAWNED is a false fact the scheduler then acts on.

THE INFORMATION NOW EXISTS AND IS BEING DISCARDED. task-89071eb1 (DONE) made the spawner refuse properly: apps/daemon/src/orchestrator/agent-spawner.ts:71 validates the command line BEFORE minting the credential, and agent-spawner.test.ts:229 pins the refusal as `code: "SPAWN_ARGUMENT_UNQUOTABLE"`. So a real, coded refusal is produced one layer down and then thrown away by the blanket catch above. This task is strictly the consumption half.

THE FIX IS SMALL AND THE TYPE ALREADY ALLOWS IT. agent-wrapper.ts:74 already declares `readonly outcome: "SPAWNED" | string;` — the report shape can carry a non-SPAWNED outcome today. No contract change is needed to report the refusal; only the reporting logic hardcodes success.

PROVENANCE: raised by governor-18a42000's adversarial audit of today's diff (7 lenses, 35 findings, 36 independent skeptic verdicts). This finding survived BOTH skeptics with ZERO kills — the strongest result in that sweep — and I re-verified it on current bytes myself. It was posted as a comment on task-89071eb1 asking that it be fixed there or explicitly deferred in writing. That task landed touching only agent-spawner.ts and its test, never agent-wrapper.ts, with no deferral recorded. Filing it here so the second clause is not lost — the same half-fix pattern that produced task-70b6361d.

NOT IN SCOPE: the spawner's own refusal (already correct), the DEP0190 command-line build, the UNQUOTABLE character set, the credential-minting order, or the wrapper's polling loop.

Verification: pnpm --filter @moe/daemon typecheck && pnpm --filter @moe/daemon test.
